## Testing Best Practices

### 1. Test Organization
- Use descriptive test method names with `@DisplayName`
- Group related tests in test classes
- Use `@Nested` for complex test scenarios
- Follow AAA pattern (Arrange, Act, Assert)

### 2. Mocking Strategy
- Mock external dependencies and services
- Use `@Mock` and `@InjectMocks` for unit tests
- Verify mock interactions when important
- Use realistic mock data

### 3. Test Data Management
- Use test data builders for complex objects
- Create reusable test utilities
- Use `@TestPropertySource` for test configuration
- Clean up test data after tests

### 4. Assertion Patterns
- Use descriptive assertion messages
- Test both positive and negative scenarios
- Verify exception types and messages
- Test edge cases and boundary conditions

### 5. Performance Testing
- Use `@DirtiesContext` sparingly
- Optimize test database operations
- Use `@Transactional` for test isolation
- Monitor test execution times




